# Task 7 report — recover accounted optimizer role output

Date: 2026-09-01

## Scope completed

- Added `PitOptimizerRoleAttempt`, which preserves accepted payloads but represents
  a fully accounted schema-invalid response with `payload=None`. Recovery requires
  a received response, an allowed validation code, complete authoritative
  accounting, and no retained reservation.
- Added exact, hash-chained `AuthorizationPlanSkip` records and
  `AuthorizationLedger.skip_unstarted_plans(...)`. Only the contiguous unstarted
  author/critic remainder of an invalid investigator iteration can be settled;
  skips create no reservation and carry no call, token, cost, or provider content.
- Changed authorization replay, next-call reservation, predecessor receipt
  binding, completion/early-stop verification, and finalization recovery to use
  settled plan indices. A plan slot is settled by exactly one reconciled attempt
  or authenticated skip. Accounted schema-invalid attempts consume one real call;
  skips consume zero.
- Kept the gateway one-shot. Parse, type, and input-binding rejections now finish
  durable accounting and return a content-free invalid attempt. Transport failure
  and incomplete/uncertain accounting still close terminally without retry.
- Added create-only schema-v4 invalid-role and authorization-skip artifacts. They
  contain only the sealed plan, provider facts, null payload, and authenticated
  skip records. Rejected provider content is never persisted in these artifacts.
- Generalized `RoleOutputInvalidSummary` to bind any v4 role to its deterministic
  plan slot while retaining the invalid-author XOR contract used by the critic.
- Updated existing authorization/gateway/receipt fixtures and assertions in
  place. No test file, test function, or test class was added. Task 8
  champion/branch/checkpoint control flow and Task 9 qualification were not added.

