## Trust/accounting self-review

1. Null-payload recovery cannot represent transport, before-send, provider, or
   uncertain-accounting failure. It requires a response-validation code,
   authoritative accounting source, exact usage/cost, and zero retained tokens.
2. Skip creation authenticates the trigger plan against the sealed manifest,
   requires its durable schema-invalid reconciliation, rejects active
   reservations, and atomically appends the exact remaining same-iteration plan
   slots. Skip parsing is closed over exact keys and verifies both chain hashes.
3. Replay rejects duplicate settlement, noncontiguous coverage, skip/plan role or
   iteration drift, absent or non-investigator triggers, and any attempt to bypass
   a live reservation. Completion requires the full settled plan; early stop
   requires a nonempty strict prefix.
4. Receipt binding checks provider facts, plan identity, null versus accepted
   payload digest, lifecycle commitments, and the durable audit event. A
   recoverable schema-invalid receipt cannot carry a lease terminal code.
5. Gateway parse/type/binding failures finalize before returning and make exactly
   one provider request. Incomplete or uncertain accounting retains its bounded
   reservation and remains terminal.

