## Fix round 1 — invalid author critic lineage

- `bind_controller_role_input` now authenticates the critic's accepted
  investigator plus an exact XOR of an accepted author artifact or an accounted
  schema-invalid author attempt.
- The invalid-author branch requires null author payload and manifest and an
  exact content-free `RoleOutputInvalidSummary` bound to the durable author's
  iteration, call index, role, and response-validation code. A transport or
  uncertain-accounting attempt cannot satisfy the branch.
- The accepted v4 branch independently rebuilds the author manifest from the
  authenticated author artifact and selected-parent identity. Legacy accepted
  critic lineage remains unchanged.
- Verification: production compile and Ruff passed; the focused v4 role-input
  smoke passed (`1 passed, 283 deselected`) and also rejected a tampered invalid
  summary validation code; `git diff --check` passed with only Windows line-ending
  notices.
